module asm ".ascii \22To allow your own fancy pointer type to interact with Boost.Unordered GDB pretty-printers,\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22create a pretty-printer for your own type with the following additional methods.\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22(Note, this is assuming the presence of a type alias `pointer` for the underlying\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22raw pointer type, Substitute whichever name is applicable in your case.)\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22`boost_to_address(fancy_ptr)`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * A static method, but `@staticmethod` is not required\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Parameter `fancy_ptr` of type `gdb.Value`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        * Its `.type` will be your fancy pointer type\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Returns a `gdb.Value` with the raw pointer equivalent to your fancy pointer\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        * This method should be equivalent to calling `operator->()` on your fancy pointer in C++\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22`boost_next(raw_ptr, offset)`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Parameter `raw_ptr` of type `gdb.Value`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        * Its `.type` will be `pointer`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Parameter `offset`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        * Either has integer type, or is of type `gdb.Value` with an underlying integer\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Returns a `gdb.Value` with the raw pointer equivalent to your fancy pointer, as if you did the following operations\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        1. Convert the incoming raw pointer to your fancy pointer\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        2. Use operator+= to add the offset to the fancy pointer\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        3. Convert back to the raw pointer\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    * Note, you will not actually do these operations as stated. You will do equivalent lower-level operations that emulate having done the above\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        * Ultimately, it will be as if you called `operator+()` on your fancy pointer in C++, but using only raw pointers\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22Example\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22```\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22class MyFancyPtrPrinter:\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    # Equivalent to `operator->()`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    def boost_to_address(fancy_ptr):\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        return ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    # Equivalent to `operator+()`\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    def boost_next(raw_ptr, offset):\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22        return ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22    ...\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22```\\n\22"
module asm ".ascii \22\\\22\\\22\\\22\\n\22"
module asm ".byte 0"
module asm ".popsection"

